rlm-pr-find [DIR] [-r|--refresh] [-d|--depth N]

Recursively find every git checkout under DIR (default: the current
directory), look up the GitHub PR whose head branch is that checkout's
CURRENT branch, and cd to the one you pick from an fzf picker.

Where rlm-pr-list covers a single repo or one collection dir and prints
a table, rlm-pr-find scans a whole tree. Run from ~/git/work it walks
every repo root AND every linked worktree — around 100 checkouts, of
which roughly a quarter have a PR.

Only checkouts that HAVE a PR are listed; this is a "jump to the repo
behind a PR" tool, so a repo without one is not a destination. Rows
show the repo, the PR number, its state (open / draft / merged /
closed, color-coded) and the PR title. The preview pane runs
`gh pr view` for the focused row, and ENTER cds to that checkout.

A repo basename alone is ambiguous — a collection dir holds one
worktree per repo, so data-platform-dbt occurs once per active ticket.
Basenames that repeat are prefixed with their parent dir, elided from
the left to keep the column narrow; unique top-level repos stay bare.

Because the scan issues one `gh` call per checkout (fanned out 16 at a
time, about 7s for 100 checkouts) results are CACHED per scan root, so
later runs open instantly. The first row of the picker is a
"--- REFRESH SCAN (scanned 12m ago) ---" sentinel that rescans and
reopens the picker. Rows are ordered most-recently-picked first, then
by newest PR update; the MRU history survives a refresh.

ARGUMENTS
  DIR              Directory to scan. Defaults to the current directory.
  -r, --refresh    Rescan before opening the picker, ignoring the cache.
  -d, --depth N    Max search depth for the checkout scan (default 4).
                   Depth 3 is needed for collection dirs; raise it only
                   if your checkouts nest deeper.
  -h, --help       Print a usage line.

FILES
  ~/.cache/rlm-pr-find/<md5 of scan root>.tsv   cached scan result
  ~/.cache/rlm-pr-find/history.txt              MRU picks, all roots

KEYS
  TAB          multi-select
  Enter        cd to the selected checkout
  Shift-up/dn  scroll the preview
  Alt-up/dn    half-page scroll the preview
  Ctrl-P       cycle preview size (70% / 40% / hidden)
  Ctrl-G       abort

REQUIRES
  gh, git, jq, fd, fzf
